Just out of habit, I do the protection run on every game I play (lately
as a Lawful Archeologist).  I manage to make it to Minetown about 7 out
of 10 times at XL1.  The problem with the Mines is that there are too
many avenues of attack and it is too hard to keep your pet between you
and your enemies.  I find it best to stay in the main dungeons all the
way down to Sokoban for the food.  Then once I'm there I do the puzzles
until the giant mimics.  Then I go back up and collect 5-10k in gold
from the shops and then descend into the mines with 1 - 3 level 9
domestic pets.  I use the wands that I find to engrave and I pray
heavily.

The advantage to this is that by building up your pets in a safer
environment (corridors and doorways) they are better able to defend you
when in the mines.  After all, the dungeon level of Minetown is not
that different than Sokoban, so it's better to be prepared.

Perhaps not too efficient or necessary but I've learned a lot from
doing this method and it works for me now so I stick with it.



